IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-damages`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"); a question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act speaks to courts ("a court cannot award", "is not liable") about a claim between two people:
--   - the injured person claiming damages: the baseline's seat (cla-damages.l4). Each answer is the baseline export's
--     own answer, wrapped in this layer's answer types;
--   - the person, or the business, the claim is made against: the defendant. Part 1A's rules are written for them
--     (ss 5B, 5H, 5I, 5J, 5O, 5P: "is not liable", "does not owe a duty"), and Part 2's limits cap what they can be
--     ordered to pay. They ask the same rules from the other side: does the Act cover the claim, what can be awarded
--     against me, does an obvious risk, my risk warning or my contract term defeat the claim. The answers the baseline
--     words for the injured person ("no duty to warn me") are reworded for the defendant.
-- The court, the Minister and the insurer are never a seat. The plaintiff's lawyer (Part 3, touting) is out of scope,
-- as in the baseline.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it is
-- FALSE, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the same name, type and
-- @desc for both roles. All four are BOOLEAN; FALSE gives does not arise:
--   - `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`: the three rules of Part 1A Division 4 (ss 5E-5J): the
--     obvious risk of a dangerous recreational activity (s 5H), a risk warning (s 5I), a term of a contract for
--     recreational services (s 5J). Each is tied to a "recreational activity" (s 5E);
--   - `the injured person was intoxicated when the harm was caused`: the presumption of contributory negligence (s 5L);
--   - `the injured person has lost earnings`: the two s 11 questions (the weekly cap and how much counts);
--   - `the injured person is cared for without charge`: gratuitous home care (s 12).
-- The questions of whether the Act and Part 2 reach the claim, the indexed amounts (s 4), general damages (s 9), the
-- general duty (s 5B), contributory negligence (s 5K) and obvious and inherent risk (ss 5N-5P) arise for every claim and
-- take none. Whether a risk was "obvious" (ss 5F, 5N, 5O) stays an ordinary input: it is the court's finding inside the
-- rule, not the occasion for asking it.
--
-- The rules are in cla-damages.l4. This module calls them and restates none. Its helpers only reword answers. The
-- defendant's questions take the baseline's records (`My claim`, `My own conduct`, `The recreational facts`, `The
-- warning`), whose items are worded as the injured person would answer them; their @desc says so. No exported question
-- takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I was injured and am claiming damages`
    `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

-- The baseline's own answer types, with `does not arise for you`; they are worded for no one seat.
DECLARE `Which of Part 1A applies, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Part 1A for me`

DECLARE `Which limits apply, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `The limits on my damages`

-- s 5O, worded for each seat.
DECLARE `A duty to warn, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `A duty to warn me`

DECLARE `My duty to warn` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `you had no duty to warn the injured person of an obvious risk (s 5O)`
    `s 5O does not take away your duty to warn, if you had one; the general law decides`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The baseline's general damages answer is always JUST an amount (s 9 never leaves it open); NOTHING cannot arise.
GIVEN `the answer` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`as an amount` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN JUST n THEN amount n
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `does not arise for you`

-- Lists every value, with no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `A duty to warn me`
GIVETH A `My duty to warn`
`for the defendant, the warning answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `no duty to warn me of an obvious risk (s 5O)` THEN `you had no duty to warn the injured person of an obvious risk (s 5O)`
    WHEN `s 5O does not take away a duty to warn; the general law decides` THEN `s 5O does not take away your duty to warn, if you had one; the general law decides`

§§ `For the injured person claiming damages`

§§§ `ss 3A, 5A, 6 -- does the Act reach the claim`

@export Which of the Civil Liability Act's liability rules (Part 1A) apply to my claim (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 3A, 5A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Which of Part 1A applies, if it arises`
`Which of Part 1A applies to the claim I make` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `the answer is` (`Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `the claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do the Civil Liability Act's limits on damages (Part 2) apply to my claim, or does another Act's (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 3, 3A, 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Which limits apply, if it arises`
`Which limits apply to the damages I claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `the answer is` (`Which limits apply to my damages` `the claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4, 9, 11, 12 -- what can be awarded`

@export What is Amount A, B or C for the next financial year, given this year's amount and the change in the WA Wage Price Index (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amount for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER @desc Amount A, B or C for the preceding financial year, in dollars
      `the WPI change in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage by which the WA Wage Price Index varied between the two December quarters
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the indexed amount for the year, as I claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN amount (`The indexed amount for the year` `the amount for the preceding year` `the WPI change in per cent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much can I be awarded for pain and suffering and loss of enjoyment of life -- general damages (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the assessed loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of the injured person's non-pecuniary loss, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much general damages can be awarded to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `as an amount` (`How much general damages can I be awarded` `the amounts` `the assessed loss`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my general damages claim below the threshold, so that I get nothing for pain and suffering (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 9(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the assessed loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of the injured person's non-pecuniary loss, in dollars
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the general damages I claim below the threshold` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `yes if` (`Is my general damages claim below the threshold` `the amounts` `the assessed loss`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a week of lost earnings that can count towards my damages (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person has lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has caused, or will cause, the injured person a loss of earnings (s 11)
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most a week of my lost earnings that can count` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person has lost earnings`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`The weekly earnings cap` `the amounts`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of my lost earnings can count towards my damages (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person has lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has caused, or will cause, the injured person a loss of earnings (s 11)
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the weekly earnings lost` IS A NUMBER @desc What the injured person would have earned a week but for the injury, in dollars
      `weeks lost` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of earnings were or will be lost
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of my lost earnings can count` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person has lost earnings`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much lost earnings can count` `the amounts` `the weekly earnings lost` `weeks lost`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much can I be awarded for care my family or household gives me without charge (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person is cared for without charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether family, household members or others care for the injured person, or will, without charging for it (s 12)
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the care would have been given anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the care would have been given even without the injury
      `hours of care a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the care is or will be given
      `weeks of care` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks
      `the value assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's valuation of the care, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much can I be awarded for care given to me without charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person is cared for without charge`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much for gratuitous home care` `the amounts` `the care would have been given anyway` `hours of care a week` `weeks of care` `the value assessed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 1A -- liability, contributory negligence, recreation and risk`

@export Can the person who hurt me be liable for failing to take precautions against the risk (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the findings` IS A `The court's findings on the risk` @desc Whether the court finds the risk foreseeable, not insignificant, and one a reasonable person would have guarded against
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the person who hurt me be liable for not taking precautions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `yes if` (`Can they be liable for not taking precautions` `the findings`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I presumed to have been partly to blame because I was intoxicated (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5L)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was intoxicated when the harm was caused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was under the influence of alcohol or a drug when the harm was caused (s 5L)
      `the injured person's conduct` IS A `My own conduct` @desc The court's findings on the injured person's own precautions, and whether they were intoxicated (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I presumed partly to blame because I was intoxicated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was intoxicated when the harm was caused`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I presumed contributorily negligent` `the injured person's conduct`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Will I be held contributorily negligent -- partly to blame for my own injury (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 5K, 5L)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `the injured person's conduct` IS A `My own conduct` @desc The court's findings on the injured person's own precautions, and whether they were intoxicated (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will I be held partly to blame for my own injury` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `yes if` (`Will I be held contributorily negligent` `the claim` `the injured person's conduct`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the rule on obvious risks of dangerous recreational activities defeat my claim (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 5E-5H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was doing a recreational activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was hurt while doing a sport, or something else for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure (s 5E)
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `facts` IS A `The recreational facts` @desc What the injured person was doing, whether the risk was significant and obvious, and whether they asked about it or had to be warned (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat the claim I make` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat my claim` `the claim` `facts`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does a risk warning defeat my claim for an injury in a recreational activity (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5I)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was doing a recreational activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was hurt while doing a sport, or something else for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure (s 5E)
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `facts` IS A `The recreational facts` @desc What the injured person was doing, whether the risk was significant and obvious, and whether they asked about it or had to be warned (worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `w` IS A `The warning` @desc Who was warned, how and by whom, the injured person's age, and what else happened (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a risk warning defeat the claim I make` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does a risk warning defeat my claim` `the claim` `facts` `w`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away my claim (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5J)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was doing a recreational activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was hurt while doing a sport, or something else for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure (s 5E)
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `facts` IS A `The recreational facts` @desc What the injured person was doing, whether the risk was significant and obvious, and whether they asked about it or had to be warned (worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `the contract excludes liability or says the injured person takes part at their own risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract for the recreational services has a term excluding or limiting liability, or saying the injured person takes part at their own risk
      `the harm resulted from breach of a personal safety law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm resulted from breach of a law setting specific safety practices or procedures
      `the harm resulted from reckless disregard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm resulted from an act or omission of the defendant in reckless disregard of its consequences
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away my claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the contract take away my claim` `the claim` `facts` `the contract excludes liability or says the injured person takes part at their own risk` `the harm resulted from breach of a personal safety law` `the harm resulted from reckless disregard`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I taken to have been aware of the risk that injured me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5N)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `it was an obvious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in the injured person's position
      `the injured person proves they were not aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person can prove they were not aware even of the type or kind of risk
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I taken to have been aware of the risk that injured me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `yes if` (`Am I presumed aware of the risk` `the claim` `it was an obvious risk` `the injured person proves they were not aware of it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Did the person who hurt me have to warn me of the risk (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5O)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `it was an obvious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in the injured person's position
      `the injured person had asked about the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person had asked the defendant for advice or information about the risk
      `a written law required a warning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written law required the defendant to warn the injured person of the risk
      `it was a risk of a professional service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant is a professional and the risk came from their professional service
GIVETH AN `A duty to warn, if it arises`
`Did the person who hurt me have to warn me of the risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `the answer is` (`Did they have to warn me` `the claim` `it was an obvious risk` `the injured person had asked about the risk` `a written law required a warning` `it was a risk of a professional service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the inherent-risk rule defeat my claim (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5P)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `it could not have been avoided by reasonable skill and care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm came from something the defendant could not have avoided with reasonable skill and care
      `the claim is that a warning was not given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a failure to warn of the risk
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the inherent risk rule defeat the claim I make` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I was injured and am claiming damages` THEN `yes if` (`Does the inherent risk rule defeat my claim` `the claim` `it could not have been avoided by reasonable skill and care` `the claim is that a warning was not given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person, or the business, the claim is made against`

§§§ `ss 3A, 5A, 6 -- does the Act reach the claim against me`

@export Which of the Civil Liability Act's liability rules (Part 1A) apply to the claim against me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 3A, 5A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Which of Part 1A applies, if it arises`
`Which of Part 1A applies to the claim against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `the answer is` (`Which of Part 1A applies to my claim` `the claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do the Civil Liability Act's limits on damages (Part 2) apply to the claim against me, or does another Act's (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 3, 3A, 6)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Which limits apply, if it arises`
`Which limits apply to the damages claimed against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `the answer is` (`Which limits apply to my damages` `the claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4, 9, 11, 12 -- what can be awarded against me`

@export What is Amount A, B or C for the next financial year, for a claim against me, given this year's amount and the change in the WA Wage Price Index (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amount for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER @desc Amount A, B or C for the preceding financial year, in dollars
      `the WPI change in per cent` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage by which the WA Wage Price Index varied between the two December quarters
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the indexed amount for the year, as the claim is against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN amount (`The indexed amount for the year` `the amount for the preceding year` `the WPI change in per cent`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much can be awarded against me for the injured person's pain and suffering and loss of enjoyment of life -- general damages (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 9)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the assessed loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of the injured person's non-pecuniary loss, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much general damages can be awarded against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `as an amount` (`How much general damages can I be awarded` `the amounts` `the assessed loss`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the general damages claim against me below the threshold, so that nothing is awarded for pain and suffering (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 9(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the assessed loss` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's assessment of the injured person's non-pecuniary loss, in dollars
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the general damages claimed against me below the threshold` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `yes if` (`Is my general damages claim below the threshold` `the amounts` `the assessed loss`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a week of the injured person's lost earnings that can count towards damages against me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person has lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has caused, or will cause, the injured person a loss of earnings (s 11)
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most a week of the injured person's lost earnings that can count against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person has lost earnings`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`The weekly earnings cap` `the amounts`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of the injured person's lost earnings can count towards damages against me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person has lost earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has caused, or will cause, the injured person a loss of earnings (s 11)
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the weekly earnings lost` IS A NUMBER @desc What the injured person would have earned a week but for the injury, in dollars
      `weeks lost` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of earnings were or will be lost
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of the injured person's lost earnings can count against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person has lost earnings`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much lost earnings can count` `the amounts` `the weekly earnings lost` `weeks lost`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much can be awarded against me for care given to the injured person without charge (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 12)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person is cared for without charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether family, household members or others care for the injured person, or will, without charging for it (s 12)
      `the amounts` IS A `The amounts for the year` @desc Amounts A, B and C and the WA average weekly earnings figures for the year
      `the care would have been given anyway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the care would have been given even without the injury
      `hours of care a week` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours a week the care is or will be given
      `weeks of care` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many weeks
      `the value assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc The court's valuation of the care, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much can be awarded against me for care given without charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person is cared for without charge`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE amount (`How much for gratuitous home care` `the amounts` `the care would have been given anyway` `hours of care a week` `weeks of care` `the value assessed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 1A -- liability, contributory negligence, recreation and risk`

@export Can I be liable for failing to take precautions against the risk that injured the person (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the findings` IS A `The court's findings on the risk` @desc Whether the court finds the risk foreseeable, not insignificant, and one a reasonable person would have guarded against
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be liable for not taking precautions against the risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `yes if` (`Can they be liable for not taking precautions` `the findings`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the injured person presumed to have been partly to blame because they were intoxicated (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5L)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was intoxicated when the harm was caused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was under the influence of alcohol or a drug when the harm was caused (s 5L)
      `the injured person's conduct` IS A `My own conduct` @desc The court's findings on the injured person's own precautions, and whether they were intoxicated (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the injured person presumed partly to blame for being intoxicated` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was intoxicated when the harm was caused`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I presumed contributorily negligent` `the injured person's conduct`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Will the injured person be held contributorily negligent -- partly to blame for their own injury (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 5K, 5L)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `the injured person's conduct` IS A `My own conduct` @desc The court's findings on the injured person's own precautions, and whether they were intoxicated (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Will the injured person be held partly to blame for their own injury` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `yes if` (`Will I be held contributorily negligent` `the claim` `the injured person's conduct`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the rule on obvious risks of dangerous recreational activities defeat the claim against me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) ss 5E-5H)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was doing a recreational activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was hurt while doing a sport, or something else for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure (s 5E)
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `facts` IS A `The recreational facts` @desc What the injured person was doing, whether the risk was significant and obvious, and whether they asked about it or had to be warned (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat the claim against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does the dangerous recreational activity rule defeat my claim` `the claim` `facts`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my risk warning defeat the claim against me for an injury in a recreational activity (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5I)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was doing a recreational activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was hurt while doing a sport, or something else for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure (s 5E)
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `facts` IS A `The recreational facts` @desc What the injured person was doing, whether the risk was significant and obvious, and whether they asked about it or had to be warned (worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `w` IS A `The warning` @desc Who was warned, how and by whom, the injured person's age, and what else happened (worded as the injured person would answer it)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a risk warning defeat the claim against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does a risk warning defeat my claim` `the claim` `facts` `w`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away the claim against me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5J)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the injured person was doing a recreational activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person was hurt while doing a sport, or something else for enjoyment, relaxation or leisure (s 5E)
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `facts` IS A `The recreational facts` @desc What the injured person was doing, whether the risk was significant and obvious, and whether they asked about it or had to be warned (worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `the contract excludes liability or says the injured person takes part at their own risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract for the recreational services has a term excluding or limiting liability, or saying the injured person takes part at their own risk
      `the harm resulted from breach of a personal safety law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm resulted from breach of a law setting specific safety practices or procedures
      `the harm resulted from reckless disregard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm resulted from an act or omission of the defendant in reckless disregard of its consequences
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can a term in my contract for recreational services take away the claim against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN
        IF NOT `the injured person was doing a recreational activity`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Can the contract take away my claim` `the claim` `facts` `the contract excludes liability or says the injured person takes part at their own risk` `the harm resulted from breach of a personal safety law` `the harm resulted from reckless disregard`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the injured person taken to have been aware of the risk that injured them (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5N)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `it was an obvious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in the injured person's position
      `the injured person proves they were not aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person can prove they were not aware even of the type or kind of risk
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is the injured person taken to have been aware of the risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `yes if` (`Am I presumed aware of the risk` `the claim` `it was an obvious risk` `the injured person proves they were not aware of it`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Did I have to warn the injured person of the risk (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5O)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `it was an obvious risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk would have been obvious to a reasonable person in the injured person's position
      `the injured person had asked about the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person had asked the defendant for advice or information about the risk
      `a written law required a warning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a written law required the defendant to warn the injured person of the risk
      `it was a risk of a professional service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant is a professional and the risk came from their professional service
GIVETH A `My duty to warn`
`Did I have to warn the injured person of the risk` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `for the defendant, the warning answer` (`Did they have to warn me` `the claim` `it was an obvious risk` `the injured person had asked about the risk` `a written law required a warning` `it was a risk of a professional service`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does the inherent-risk rule defeat the claim against me (Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) s 5P)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the claim` IS A `My claim` @desc What caused the injury, when it happened, and whether the claim is a motor vehicle (CTP) or workers' compensation claim against the employer (each item worded as the injured person would answer it)
      `it could not have been avoided by reasonable skill and care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the harm came from something the defendant could not have avoided with reasonable skill and care
      `the claim is that a warning was not given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for a failure to warn of the risk
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the inherent risk rule defeat the claim against me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `A claim for damages for an injury is made against me` THEN `yes if` (`Does the inherent risk rule defeat my claim` `the claim` `it could not have been avoided by reasonable skill and care` `the claim is that a warning was not given`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
